# DataCareNext API — environment configuration (copy to .env; never commit real secrets).

# --- Database ---
# Runtime MUST use the non-superuser app_user so Row-Level Security is enforced.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://app_user:CHANGE_ME@postgres:5432/datacare
# Migration/owner connection (DDL, prisma migrate) — superuser-ish role:
MIGRATE_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://datacare:CHANGE_ME@postgres:5432/datacare
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME      # postgres superuser (compose)
APP_DB_PASSWORD=CHANGE_ME        # app_user password (compose interpolates into DATABASE_URL)

# --- Auth ---
JWT_SECRET=CHANGE_ME_long_random_string   # injected into buildApp({secret})

# --- Cache / queue (right-sized; optional) ---
REDIS_URL=redis://redis:6379

# --- App ---
PORT=3000
APP_VERSION=0.0.0
APP_TENANT_ID=default  # must match the migrated customer's tenant_id
NODE_ENV=production

# --- Messaging (WhatsApp Cloud API or an HTTP SMS gateway) ---
# Leave blank to keep messaging OFF: with neither provider configured the API refuses every send (HTTP 503) and
# records nothing; it never pretends a message was sent. These are the names the code reads
# (apps/api/src/modules/integrations/messaging.ts). Earlier revisions documented WHATSAPP_TOKEN /
# WHATSAPP_PHONE_ID / SMS_API_KEY, which nothing reads, and the compose file did not forward any of them.
# WA_PHONE_ID=           # WhatsApp Cloud API phone-number id
# WA_TOKEN=              # WhatsApp Cloud API bearer token
# WA_API_VERSION=        # optional Graph API version (default in code)
# SMS_URL_TEMPLATE=      # gateway URL with {key} {sender} {mobile} {text} placeholders
# SMS_KEY=
# SMS_SENDER=            # optional sender/header id
# Never set MESSAGING_FAKE_MODE here: it is test-only and the API refuses to start with it in production.

# --- Observability ---
# SENTRY_DSN=            # error reporting (observability drop-in)

# --- e-Invoice / IRN (GSP: Chartered Info) ---
# THESE ARE NOT OPTIONAL IF YOU E-INVOICE. Unlike the senders above, e-invoicing has no safe no-op: a fake
# IRN written onto a real invoice makes that invoice invalid tax documentation. With NODE_ENV=production the
# API therefore REFUSES to issue an IRN unless all five credentials below are present, and refuses unless
# GSP_SANDBOX states sandbox-vs-production explicitly.
#
# A shop that does not e-invoice needs none of this — just do not call the /einvoice routes.
#
# These are the names the code actually reads (apps/api/src/modules/einvoice/einvoice.ts). Earlier revisions
# of this file documented GSP_BASE_URL / GSP_CLIENT_ID / GSP_CLIENT_SECRET, which are read by nothing: an
# operator who set those got no error and silently produced fabricated IRNs.
# GSP_ASPID=
# GSP_PASSWORD=
# GSP_GSTIN=
# GSP_USER=
# GSP_EINV_PWD=
# GSP_SANDBOX=1          # 1 = GSP sandbox (IRNs are NOT legally valid), 0 = production. Must be explicit.

# --- Backups ---
# BACKUP_DIR=/var/backups/datacare
# RETENTION_DAYS=14
